Pi icon
The Pi glyph is vendored from https://thesvg.org/icon/pi
Source: https://github.com/GLINCKER/thesvg/blob/main/public/icons/pi/default.svg
The source library's MIT notice is retained in packages/shared/assets/pi.LICENSE.
PiDeck uses the glyph in its native icons, favicon and interface mark; native
background and interface colour/animation are adaptations. This does not imply
endorsement by Pi or theSVG.

Embedded browser behavior
The browser panel and element-selection behavior are adapted from the Apache-2.0 ZCode project:
https://github.com/zai-org/ZCode, commit 3c5b227649371507ddc4eb46ac5133afe6db1cab.
References: packages/ui/src/browser-use/UnifiedBrowserView.tsx, EmbeddedBrowserPaneParts.tsx,
lib/webElementPickerScript.ts and hooks/useWebElementPicker.ts.
PiDeck reimplements the integration for Electrobun/CEF, its contracts, themes and chat drafts.
The Apache License, Version 2.0 is included in LICENSE.
Chromium/CEF licensing notices ship with the Electrobun CEF distribution.

Browser automation and recording behavior additionally reference ZCode's browser-use command metadata,
browser-client facade/Playwright API, browserGuestManager recording actions, browserVideoRecorder,
electronBrowserWebmRecorder and virtual clipboard paste behavior at the same revision.
The Pi tool/host integration, CEF input/capture adapters and WebM encoding transport are adapted for PiDeck.
Playwright core is distributed under Apache-2.0; its LICENSE and NOTICE accompany the staged package.
